//@ run-pass
//@ timeout: 300
//@ expect-stdout-contains: M2_HIERARCHICAL_PRIOR_PASS
//@ known-failure: measured 2026-09-22 under SOUNIO_SOUC_ENGINE=lean_single -- rel_Hess_individual=0.875070 and rel_Hess_population=0.873336, both far past the 0.10 criterion (M2_HIERARCHICAL_PRIOR_OUTPUT, not _PASS). Closing the vacuous PASS-regardless gate (the fix this annotation accompanies) surfaces this measured GUM/Hessian-vs-MC discrepancy in the hierarchical prior decomposition; it is a pre-existing PBPK28 numerical-methods gap, not something this review round investigates or resolves.
// mc28_hierarchical_selftest_main prints M2_HIERARCHICAL_PRIOR_OUTPUT (not
// _PASS) when individual_pass is false, but then unconditionally prints
// PASS and returns 0 regardless -- an unannotated run-pass file only checks
// the exit code, so without this it would report success even when the
// hierarchical-prior criterion actually failed. Requiring the real success
// marker closes that.
// tests/run-pass/pbpk28_m2_hierarchical_prior.sio
//
// Opt-in wrapper for PBPK28 M2 hierarchical eta/epsilon prior decomposition.
// The canonical single-level MC cross-validation remains the default main in
// stdlib/darwin_pbpk/validation/pbpk28_mc_cross_validation.sio.

use darwin_pbpk::validation::pbpk28_mc_cross_validation::{mc28_hierarchical_selftest_main}

fn main() -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    mc28_hierarchical_selftest_main()
}
